A||||11||Roy||Got A Speeding Ticket In My Fiero
Z||000000||Roy||07-21-99||05:19 PM||||Sorry that this is a little bit off topic didn't know where else I might get some help.Hey guys, I was wondering if any of you knew much about laser radar. I was crusing down the street going 35 in a 30. A cop tagged me with a laser. He claims I was going 42. But I have a digital spedometer and I know I was going 35. I was just wondering if anyone knew anyway to get out of this? There was very light fog and it was 9:30 at night, there were cars on all sides of me. I can't get another ticket, And I know for a fact I wasnt speeding.<p>Roy
Z||000001||PaUL||07-21-99||08:57 PM||||well Roy, you should contest the citation. My friend is a cop and they are all the same anywhere you go. Theyll try to pin anything they can on you but when it comes time to go before the judge the burden of proof is on them. They have to prove beyond a reasonable doubt that you are guilty. After the cop stopped you, did you DEMAND to inspect his laser/radar? You should to be sure he wasnt just making it up. You could use the fog and the other cars around you as a defense. I think laser is less effective under these conditions. If all else fails, you could say that your speed was mis-calibrated.
Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||07-21-99||09:02 PM||||Just for the record: that wasn't <b>our</b> digital speedometer!  ;)<br>
Z||000003||Roy||07-21-99||11:08 PM||||Nope it wasnt yours cliff:)<p>Next pay check I should be buying yours.<br>
Z||000004||batboy||07-21-99||11:20 PM||||Roy, Roy, Roy! One minute you said you were doing 35 in a 30 zone and the next minute you said you weren't speeding. I'm confused. Doing 5 over the limit is not speeding? But, I know what you mean. I'd go to court like Paul said, if for some reason the cop don't show up to testify, the judge will throw the ticket out (this happens, but not real often). Don't mention the fog, that might go against you. The judge might say you should of been going much less than the speed limit in the fog. Do you have bigger tires than the originals? This will cause your speedometer (digital or not) to register slower than you are actually going. Go out on the highway with mile markers, drive a steady 60 mph and have a friend with a stop watch time you between mileposts. If you are hitting the mile markers at exactly 60 second intervals, your speedo is accurate. Less than 60 seconds means you are going faster than 60 mph and your speedo is off. Don't DEMAND to see the locked in speed on the radar or laser, the cop will think you're a smart-ass and give you a hard time or write you another ticket for some other lame reason. ASK politely to see the reading, they are supposed to let you see it if you request it. I did this once and the cop finally admitted he didn't have it locked in (I slowed too quick when I saw him for him to lock it in) so he let me off with a warning. I've gotten out of several tickets for being polite and honest (never lie to a cop, they hate it because they get lied to all the time and feel that it's an insult to their intelligence). In court, ask the judge to have the officer to produce the calibration log. Cops are required to calibrate the radar/laser at certain defined intervals and keep a record of this. You might need to find out before hand what that interval is in your locale. Finally, point out that there were other cars in the immediate area that the officer may have clocked and accidently assumed it was you. I've heard of tickets getting thrown out if you can prove there was a lot of traffic around you. I've gotten an unjustified speeding ticket once, so I know how you feel.
Z||000005||kel||07-21-99||11:47 PM||||Well a few years ago, I was driving on an Interstate, had my cruise set at 55 mph (that was the speed limit then) and saw a cop sitting on one of the on-ramps.  I was going down a bit of a hill, but didn't think anything of it.  This green PINTO passed me and I saw the cop coming down the ramp.  He turned on his lights and siren and pulled ME over!  Said I was going 57 mph, and the speed limit was 55!  Said he would just give me a warning this time. (Gee thanks)<br>I actually have alot of respect for police officers (I shoot with them all the time at the shooting range) but that was uncalled for.  (Ya think he just wanted to get a better look at my beautiful car???)
Z||000006||lowCG||07-22-99||12:45 AM||||Most cops had lousy childhoods,that's why they wind up trying to protect people(FU@*ED- UP)but anyways,Batboy is correct in trying to maintain a proper channel of communication between you and the officer;after all,it can only get worse.<br>You have to know when to admit you may have been at fault,however,(then explain the circumstances)but you INTENTIONS were to be going the indicated speed limit.Then it's up to whoever you're trying to convince to decide whether you're trying to get away with something in a devious manner.Faulty equipment,ie.  bad speedometer,is not a valid excuse,however.<br>Justice is a strange thing sometimes.<br>Reminds me,that it's time to go pay my attorney some more $...<br>
Z||000007||Cliff Pennock||07-22-99||05:52 AM||||Kel, I got pulled over by the cops once. They made me open the engine compartment, looked inside the car, under the car, etc. When I asked them why I was pulled over they said: "we're sorry to have pulled you over sir, but we really wanted to have a good look at your car - it's beautiful!".<p>Yes, cops are only human after all...
Z||000008||ChadMan||07-22-99||07:15 AM||||I once beat a bullcrap ticket merely by showing up to court to fight it - the cop didn't show up.  Automatic win for me.  I still had to pay my lawyer $200 for showing up, but that ticket would have put me into high-risk rates, so it was worth it.<p>Maybe you'll get lucky, Roy, and your cop will be staking out a Krispy Kreme while the judge dismisses your case!
Z||000009||jaybailey||07-22-99||10:09 AM||||You certainly don't need a lawyer to go to court to fight a speeding ticket.  First, and foremost, request a written deposition of the incident.  If the officer doesn't supply one (most won't because its extra paper work) then the case will be dismissed.  Second, if you show up in court and the officer doesn't you win.  Third, if all else fails, tell your story, say you weren't speeding and see what happens.  I've had several moving violations and I've never been convicted of any of them with these techniques.
Z||000010||Racer 1||07-22-99||01:51 PM||||Well well roy alittle lead foot happy are ya.Heres some ideas I thought up to dismiss those g-d forbinden traffic tickets.First of fight the ticket and get a hearing like mentioned above.Then before you go to court dress up like elvis with dark glasses and long sideburns etc.Then when MR.OFFICER gets done with his testamony.Say to the judge"Yeah judge when the cop turned his laser gun at my car it blinded me momentararley and I was scared I thought it was a UFO coming to get my car and then I gassed it alittle till I knew what the light was from".Or you could hire O.J.'s dream team and get the ticket dismissed.Theres always ways around stuff you just need to be creative with your words and throw in some bs'ing.Good Luck
Z||000011||Roy||07-23-99||04:19 AM||||Ok just for the persons who were saying why I was saying I wasnt speeding, I was going 35 in a 30. Everyone knows you are given a 5mph buffer. Photo Radar is set to snap your picture at anything above five where I live. 
